    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10046" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conductīcĭus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		conduco, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to hire,
				hired, rented</i> (rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fidicina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Ep. 2, 3, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">5, 2, 41</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i>
			 arg. 2: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exercitus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep. Iphicr. 2, 4</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">catervae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Chabr. 1, 2</span></i>
			: domus, Porcius, poët. ap. <i><span class="en">Suet. Vit. Ter. 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">operae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 17, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
